, "side": false, "subagent": false, "provider": null, "requested": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "served": {"claude-sonnet-5-5": 1}, "parameters": {"max_tokens": 128000, "output_config.effort": "high", "thinking.display": "summarized", "thinking.type": "adaptive"}, "tools": ["Agent", "Bash", "Edit", "Read", "Skill", "TaskStop", "WebFetch", "Write", "mcp__rwe-search__search_literature"], "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 1461, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 1461, "cached_input": 71381, "input": 72844, "output": 132}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 101493, "other": 423, "system": 31058, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 92020}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 239391}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "40cec4a4-ae1e-5104-95f3-0a05a9e4bb76", "at": 1795671370.7549813, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 14586, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "a9c715cc5714e28eac7bda1297f5d485", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "60141193-c135-5ac6-9586-d4e7fad6c3ce", "at": 1795671370.7605126, "until": 1795671372.403734, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 14587, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "a9c715cc5714e28eac7bda1297f5d485", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01PXuh9fobWv52RTNQdzj7oC", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/storywiki; git remote set-url origin $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git; git pull -q 2>&1|tail -1; git log --oneline|head -3; git diff 0912470 HEAD", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/storywiki; git remote set-url origin $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git; git pull -q 2>&1|tail -1; git log --oneline|head -3; git diff 0912470 HEAD"]], "output": "```console\n9bca2fb Fit the outline to the NeurIPS budget: 7 main items, General contribution type\n0912470 Revise the outline after idea review: nested tuning, per-target bias unit, minimum Tier-2 rule, theory-check ceiling, source-count analysis, CAT protocol, fixed primary and secondary n\n81659ca Clarify the figure message and the contribution mapping\ndiff --git a/Outline.md b/Outline.md\nindex 6e9e17c..2535d71 100644\n--- a/Outline.md\n+++ b/Outline.md\n@@ -1,7 +1,10 @@\n-# Outline (revision 2, after idea-review #3) — story-repo\n+# Outline (revision 3, after idea-review #3 and venue #4) — story-repo\n \n Working from: `Brief` of idea-repo (revision 2), objective `story-repo#1`. This page says **what to test and what each part of the paper says**; it never says what a result must be. Where a result decides between two stories, both are written below (§6) so nobody has to rewrite the paper's frame after the fact.\n \n+## Venue frame (venue-repo, `story-repo`#4)\n+NeurIPS 2026 Main Track; **9 content pages including figures and tables**; references, appendix and checklist outside. **Contribution type: General** (an evaluation paper: controlled comparison, bias–variance accounting, ceiling analysis), also if the headline turns out conditional or negative: \"Negative Results\" is not chosen (high significance/originality bar). **Main body: 7 items** — Fig. 1, Table 2, Fig. 2, Fig. 3, Fig. 4, Fig. 5, Fig. 6 (Fig. 1 is a small schematic). Everything else is appendix: Table 1 (audit and split/target counts), Table 3, Table 4, Fig. 5b, per-benchmark tables. Evidence a claim rests on is in the main body: the main text carries the k targets / #families per split in Table 2's columns and one sentence on thin cells, and says where Table 1 is. Writing profile: abstract one paragraph ≈ 130–260 words stating claims, scope and the headline; introduction ≈ 550–1500 words with the result stated; first figure on page 1–2; short related work in the main text, long version in the appendix; the checklist's \"Claims\" item is checked against the evidence.\n+\n ## 0. The paper in one paragraph\n Evaluating an LLM on a full benchmark is costly, so we run it on n ≪ N items and predict its full score. Existing methods (anchor points, tinyBenchmarks, metabench, assessor, active acquisition) use the score matrix of *source models* to pick items and fit a *latent model* of the target; they are judged mostly on held-out models that resemble the sources. We cast the problem as **finite-population estimation of a mean of N unknown 0/1 values with a free covariate (the source matrix)**. That frame separates what the sources can buy — **variance reduction** — from what must be controlled by design — **bias**. We (i) test, on 13 binary matrices and under three target splits (interpolation, extrapolation, lineage-held-out), whether model-based predictors lose accuracy where targets differ from the sources; (ii) test whether a design-based correction (probability sampling with a positivity floor + difference/GREG estimator) repairs it and at what variance cost; (iii) measure how much the source matrix can help at all over plain stratified/balanced random sampling; (iv) examine ordering of models separately from score error. A negative or conditional answer to any of these is a result.\n \n@@ -17,10 +20,10 @@ Primary endpoint (fixed before running): **RMSE ratio to uniform random sampling\n | C2 | **Bias–variance:** model-based predictors show signed bias that grows away from the source range (compression toward the source mean); the difference estimator removes it and costs a stated amount of variance — or it does not | Signed error vs true score per method class, extrapolation split especially; bias and variance computed **per target over subset draws first (≥100 draws where cheap), then summarised across targets**, with the Monte Carlo SE of each per-target bias shown (no pooling of targets and draws into one \"variance\"); λ, ε tuned on sources only **with a tuning split that mimic\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "9b1d00c0-9c9f-5c74-897d-729539488d50", "at": 1795671371.7199414, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 14601, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "a9c715cc5714e28eac7bda1297f5d485", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "b50659e2-8ca8-59ba-8569-c362718e14c9", "at": 1795671371.7229514, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 14602, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "a9c715cc5714e28eac7bda1297f5d485", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "4c51bb29-af55-5de0-b605-82753d2d7558", "at": 1795671371.7250385, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 14603, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "a9c715cc5714e28eac7bda1297f5d485", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "0699d222-293d-591a-aed8-17eeaf0905ce", "at": 1795671371.7862012, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 14604, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "a9c715cc5714e28eac7bda1297f5d485", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "credential-required", "label": "challeng